  "answer_text": "India’s current GDP growth forecast for FY 2026–27 is about 7.0–7.1%. The Reserve Bank of India projects 7.1%, while the World Bank and OECD also forecast 7.1%; Moody’s recently revised its estimate to 7.0%.\n\nLatest forecasts\nForecaster\tFY 2026–27 real GDP growth\nReserve Bank of India\t7.1% \nWorld Bank\t7.1% \nOECD\t7.1% \nMoody’s Ratings\t7.0% \nWhy forecasts rose\nForecasters upgraded India’s outlook after strong first-quarter growth of 7.8%, resilient domestic demand, improving investment, and export strength.\n\nThe main risks are inflation and possible tighter monetary policy, which could weigh on private investment.\n\nsources shown:\nhttps://www.thehindubusinessline.com/economy/moodys-ups-growth-forecast-for-india-to-7-cautions-high-inflation/article71688879.ece\nhttps://theprint.in/economy/indian-economy-has-been-shining-star-in-otherwise-gloomy-world-niti-aayog-vc/3097209/\nhttps://www.pib.gov.in/FactsheetDetails.aspx?Id=150991&reg=3&lang=1\nhttps://economictimes.indiatimes.com/topic/Indian-GDP-growth-estimate/news\nhttps://ianslive.in/indias-gdp-growth-expected-to-reach-77-pc-in-q3-fy27-to-see-74-pc-growth-bofa--20261112133903\nnote: the interface showed \"Sources 20\"; these 5 were recovered. No inline markers in the pasted answer.\n",
